=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play environment/debian13 ------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: environment/debian13$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13, sudo 1.9.16p2. alice ran$
# sudo hardn; sudo dropped HARDN_CONFIG.$
$
# Environment Variable Settings ################################$
$
  HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [ ] Under sudo           Not kept by hardn$
   -  Value                Not set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Under sudo           Keep HARDN_CONFIG$
   2) Guide                How to set HARDN_CONFIG$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Keep HARDN_CONFIG ############################################$
$
  HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [+] Under sudo           Kept by hardn$
$
   -  Keep HARDN_CONFIG$
      /etc/sudoers.d/hardn-env-alice$
      @@ -0,0 +1,2 @@$
      +# Managed by hardn$
      +Defaults:alice env_keep += "HARDN_CONFIG"$
$
  No actual changes were made to your system.$
$
# Environment Variable Settings ################################$
$
  HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [ ] Under sudo           Not kept by hardn$
   -  Value                Not set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Under sudo           Keep HARDN_CONFIG$
   2) Guide                How to set HARDN_CONFIG$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

